en to use each rule — a brief decision-tree would help.","factors":[{"text":"Colour-coded board work made notation significantly clearer.","type":"strength"},{"text":"Step-by-step modelling reduced cognitive load for new content.","type":"strength"},{"text":"Provide a decision-tree for choosing sine vs cosine rule.","type":"improvement","technique":"Worked Examples"},{"text":"Narrate each step aloud while writing to support diverse learners.","type":"improvement","technique":"Think Aloud"}]},{"name":"formative_assessment","label":"Satisfactory","score":64,"narrative":"Finn circulated effectively during independent work and addressed errors individually. However, whole-class checks were limited to two thumbs up/down moments, providing insufficient data on overall comprehension.","factors":[{"text":"Effective circulation and one-to-one error correction during practice.","type":"strength"},{"text":"Identified and addressed a common misconception mid-lesson.","type":"strength"},{"text":"Use mini-whiteboards or show-me cards for whole-class checks.","type":"improvement","technique":"Whole-Class Response"},{"text":"Add a structured mid-lesson check before students move to independent work.","type":"improvement","technique":"Checkpoint Questions"}]},{"name":"engagement","label":"Good","score":76,"narrative":"Students were engaged during the worked examples and independent practice. The real-world context (navigation and land surveying) provided a motivating hook that several students referenced during the lesson.","factors":[{"text":"Real-world navigation context created a strong motivating hook.","type":"strength"},{"text":"Students remained on-task during the full independent practice phase.","type":"strength"},{"text":"Include a challenge extension task for early finishers.","type":"improvement","technique":"Differentiation"},{"text":"Add a brief collaborative element to the practice phase.","type":"improvement","technique":"Collaborative Learning"}]},{"name":"technology","label":"Satisfactory","score":60,"narrative":"The interactive whiteboard was used for display and annotation only. A dynamic geometry tool or graphing application would have enhanced conceptual understanding of the trigonometric relationships.","factors":[{"text":"Board annotations were clear and well-organised.","type":"strength"},{"text":"No technical disruptions; technology was reliable.","type":"strength"},{"text":"Use a dynamic geometry tool to visualise the sine and cosine rules.","type":"improvement","technique":"Dynamic Geometry Software"},{"text":"Consider a short graphing activity to connect algebra to visual representation.","type":"improvement","technique":"Data Visualisation"}]}],"performance_summary":{"key_strengths":[{"text":"Excellent behaviour management with a calm, authoritative presence","dimension":"Behaviour Management"},{"text":"Colour-coded board work and step-by-step modelling made new content accessible","dimension":"Clarity"}],"areas_for_improvement":[{"text":"Whole-class formative assessment is infrequent — individual checks miss broader patterns","dimension":"Formative Assessment"},{"text":"Technology is used passively; dynamic tools would deepen conceptual understanding","dimension":"Technology"}]}}',
